# Exclude everything; reinclude only what the Docker build needs.
# build context is panoseti-software/ (repo root)
**
!control/**
!grpc/**
!pypff/**
!sw_info.json

# Ignore dev environments and caches inside included directories
**/.venv
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
**/.git
**/tmp
**/*.ipynb
**/notebooks/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
**/docs/

# Runtime data left behind by locally-run docker-compose stacks (e.g. Loki, Grafana
# provisioning bind-mount targets) -- these are gitignored but not excluded from the
# build context above, and can contain root-owned files that break the build.
**/loki-data/
**/grafana_provisioning/

# control/state/ is PanoPaths.state_dir()'s default location -- a local run/test
# on the machine doing `docker build` leaves a real ledger, locks, and daemon logs
# there. Gitignored but (like the entries above) not excluded from the build
# context, so it was getting baked into the image verbatim: a stale
# state/logs/transfer_daemon/stderr.log from a pre-uv/miniconda interpreter showed
# up inside a freshly built container that never actually ran the transfer daemon.
**/control/state/
